.TH qmaint "1" "Sep 2026" "Gentoo Foundation" "qmaint"
.SH NAME
qmaint \- perform package management housekeeping (emaint port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qmaint
\fI[opts] <module> <action>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIqmaint\fR performs package\-management housekeeping tasks and is a C
reimplementation of Portage's \fBemaint\fR. It operates on a named
\fImodule\fR with either the \fB\-\-check\fR or \fB\-\-fix\fR action.
.P
The available modules are:
.TP
.B binhost
Check that the local \fIPKGDIR/Packages\fR index agrees with the binary
packages on disk; \fB\-\-fix\fR regenerates the index (see also
\fBqmerge\fR(1) \fB\-\-index\fR).
.TP
.B moves
Apply the outstanding package and slot moves from the repositories'
update records to the installed package database.
.TP
.B news
Reconcile GLEP\ 42 news bookkeeping (see \fBqnews\fR(1)).
.TP
.B env
Regenerate the environment (\fI/etc/profile.env\fR and friends) from
\fI/etc/env.d\fR, equivalent to \fBenv\-update\fR(1).
.P
With neither \fB\-\-check\fR nor \fB\-\-fix\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR is
assumed. A check that finds nothing prints nothing and exits
successfully: the exit status, not the output, is the result signal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR
Report problems for the given module without changing anything. No
output together with a successful exit status means no problems were
found.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fix\fR
Repair the problems that the corresponding \fB\-\-check\fR would
report. \fB\-\-check\fR and \fB\-\-fix\fR are mutually exclusive.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ldconfig\fR
\fIenv\fR module only: regenerate the environment files but do not
run \fBldconfig\fR to rebuild \fIld.so.cache\fR,matching
portage's \fBenv\-update\ \-\-no\-ldconfig\fR. Rejected for the
other modules.
.TP
\fB\-\-delete\-individual\-files\fR
vdb module, with --fix: remove the per-field files after writing the metadata file.
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
vdb module: restore per-field files and remove the metadata file (undo --fix).
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<arg>\fR
Set the ROOT env var.
.TP
\fB\-\-overlay\fR \fI<arg>\fR
Select the given overlay for use, instead of all found (see q -o).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Report full package versions, emit more elaborate output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Tighter output; suppress warnings.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-nocolor\fR
Don't output color.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR
Force color in output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit.

